I forget now after a couple of years.  What is the SCSI chip on the motherboard?
Some of the DEC boxes favored on-board Symbios Logic chips, for which XP drivers
would probably not exist.  Substitute a known SCSI adapter like an Adaptec 2940
or 2940W, and you might be ahead of the game.

What sort of graphics?  If the graphics is on-board and some sort of chip from a
defunct company, you could probably survive with the installation of a PCI card,
carefully chosen.  

Installing XP and even 2000 on some of these old boxes is a bit of a challenge
because the chip manufacturers are long gone, absorbed by another company
(Symbios has an especially checkered history), or no longer supporting a chip
(e.g. Cirrus no longer has anything to do with graphics chips.  A good thing,
too.)  ... Ben Myers

