> >Thanks,

> Maybe.  I need to check my stash.  Can you also provide the specs on it?  Is it
> that peculiar 83MHz 168-pin stuff?  How many? ... Ben Myers

Assuming "DPW" as "DEC Personal Workstation" aka MIATA...

PC100 CL2 buffered modules also work fine. Got some Micron 128MB modules
recently at eBay Germany for about 17 EUR, purchades 12 pieces and have 2
Miatas with 768MB each now. Works stable since months.

Combining all search results from Google, you need PC100, faster modules can
make trouble. And you need CL2, slower latency can also make trouble. 72bits
also are a must i think (ECC), and they must have those latches, the modules
having those are usually calles "registered", sometimes "buffered", but don't
confuse this with the module notch telling about "buffered".

If you look at the module, connectors down, one notch in the middle, one notch
left of the middle, those notches can have 3 positions.
The left notch has to be in the rightmost position (unbuffered), the middle
notch in the center position (3.3V), like all PC modules also go.

Modules with those specs should also work in XP1000. And if someone needs the
seller name for the Micron modules for eBay Germany (he has those modules quite
often), contact me in PM.

...Michael

