I wish I had been smart enough to get permission to photograph
the silkscreen shop walls at MLO. Back in the late 70s when I
was in Maynard a lot for training I used to tramp around in the
mill. If you went in the main Thompson St. entrance (north end
of the building, IIRC) and then went down a few levels right
after you entered, you ended up in/near a silkscreen shop where
they did front panels for (some? all??) systems. I saw (mostly)
PDP-11 front panels of every color - most of the 'strange'
colors were custom jobs for OEMs (and it would have their
name on it instead of DEC), or (for instance), a
red-white-and-blue front panel for an 11/45 "industrial
version".

They probably used to make an extra one to put up on the wall
from each special job.


