Hi,

I'm running an Alpha workstation based on a DEC AlphaPC 164LX
motherboard. It comes with 1GB Registered RAM and a genuine 600MHz 21164
Alpha CPU (not a 21164PC or a 21164 533@600 CPU). The graphics adapter
is a Compaq PowerStorm 300 PCI and Tru64 V5.1 is installed. In order to
quantify the improvement from my previous DEC PowerStorm 4D60T adapter,
I ran the SPEC viewperf 6.1 benchmark. I used the viewperf61 binary
built by DEC/Compaq available on the SPEC FTP server. Results are really
poor:
- AWadvs: 4.68
- DRV: 1.507
- DX: 2.284
- Light: 0.492
- ProCDRS: 1.330

With the DEC PowerStorm 4D60T, I get:
- AWadvs: 14.093
- DRV: 7.446
- DX: 12.158
- Light: 1.508
- ProCDRS: 7.018

Quite a difference indeed! IIRC, the geometry calculation is performed
by the host 21164 Alpha CPU with the Compaq PowerStorm 300, whereas a
specific ship performs this operation in hardware on the DEC PowerStorm
4D60T. Thus, I initially thought it was due to my CPU not being powerful
enough (the Compaq XP1000 Professional Workstation was generally sold
with this card). But I then found this URL
http://www.spec.org/gpc/Dec98/opc.data/opc_nov98/summary.html showing in
the 13th row a DEC PWS 600 workstation equipped with a Compaq PowerStorm
300 scoring really better results. A big difference is that the
benchmark wasn't performed under Tru64, but under Windows NT 4.0
Workstation. Other than that, the AlphaPC 164LX and PWS 600 systemboard
are very close by design. Most notably, they're based on the same 21164
CPU and have identical memory bandwith. So I don't know what can explain
the difference. The sole OS? The PCI busses topology (seem roughly
equivalent for me)? The manner the devices are organized in the PCI
busses? I mean, my Compaq PowerStorm 300 is actually installed in Slot 0
(as recommended by the Installation Notes) thus sharing the PCI bandwith
with my NCR 53c875 SCSI adapter in the 64-bit PCI bus (I here suppose
the 64-bit and 32-bit PCI busses on the AlphaPC 164LX are totally
independant. Am I wrong?). Could insufficient PCI bandwith be the reason
here? In this case, how to optimally install my graphics adapter, SCSI
HBA and network card across the two PCI busses provided by the AlphaPC
164LX motherboard?

Any (other) ideas/suggestions greatly appreciated!

Thanks


-- 
