Just one thought.  NT uses ARC/Alphabios; Tru64 uses SRM, the same as 
VMS.  For VMS, the PS300 is specifically _only_ supported on EV6 
platforms like the XP1000/DS10.  I don't have info on Tru64, but the PWS 
#00au SRM for VMS can use the PS300 as a VGA console but can't/doesn't 
initialize it for graphics.  Perhaps Tru64 is simply using it as a dumb 
VGA card without any hardware capabilities enabled because the EV5 SRM 
can't set up the card properly...


