Run diagnostics on the memory (MEMTEST-86) and the hard drive (manufacturer's
diagnostics) to see if something is failing or has failed.

Replace the C2032 3v Lithium CMOS battery.

Check and double-check jumper settings for drives.

If the hard drive is greater than 8GB in capacity, use another with less
capacity, or complicate matters somewhat by adding a Promise IDE controller.

That's all I can think of... Ben Myers

